% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `trace`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: no part of
% `trace` is printed or held, and NO TRACER IS MODELLED.  Its one method is
% INTERPOLATED (labelled) from:
%   - pimfep##as_pimos_string_io_device trace_string_io/1 (held .ptf,
%     @a5): `:trace(#trace)` as a last call, after a neck cut, with no
%     other goal (docs/simpos/subsystems/shell.md:438);
%   - kwic-esp autoTracer.esp:23 `:trace( #trace , AT!proNumber )`
%     (shell.md:437).  trace/2 takes a process number: cal-esp
%     deb2.12/util.esp:217-227, the help text "Multi_process_debugger",
%     `:trace(#trace)/:trace(#trace,Process_no)`; notrace/1 and notrace/2
%     exist (same lines) and are not stood in;
%   - TR-087 PDF p11 §5.4: the system tracer "runs as a separate process
%     and traces the execution of other processes";
%   - the debugger's trace mode, documented as a screen and its commands
%     (TM-181 pp.4-5; shell.md §3), which this stand-in does not provide.
% Model (OURS): trace/1 succeeds and does nothing.  A method that succeeds
% only through it says nothing about tracing.

class trace has

% INTERPOLATED from: the pimfep call `:trace(#trace)` (see above).  It
% does nothing: no debugger is modelled (OURS).
:trace(Class);

end.
